20,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
21,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It turns out the same people have held the best spots for years without any review. Also, complaints about bikes leaning on each other are common but never resolved.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Some households have three bikes while others have none! Interestingly, the daily riders said they'd actually prefer to pay for a spot than have equal claims.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The morning rush is a mess; people are constantly shifting other bikes to get out. Plus, the spots past the downpipe are completely exposed to rain.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Our shared account is nearly empty, so any upgrades would need a levy. Also, the ward park is expensive and has a huge waiting list.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Managing cash collections is already a three-hour monthly chore. Also, those fancy double-tier racks are physically demanding to use and need regular maintenance.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, if people are willing to pay, that might solve the fairness issue, but we have to be careful about the social atmosphere.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, it sounds like the current ""fixed"" spots are causing a lot of physical frustration in the mornings.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the fact that the same people have the dry spots for years explains why the atmosphere has gone sour.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, if the treasurer is already struggling, adding more billing for individual spots sounds like a nightmare.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"Exactly, Shunichi. Any system that increases paperwork will likely just collapse after a few months.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, if the ward park is full and expensive, we really have to find a solution within the building.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"I'm worried that if we keep the current system, the people with three bikes will just keep taking up all the space.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"If we don't fix the ""shoving match"" in the morning, the complaints will only get worse regardless of who owns the spot.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,It seems we have a conflict between those who want stability and those who want fairness.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"And we have to consider the physical effort. If a solution requires heavy lifting or constant greasing, people will stop doing it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Asuka,,We need a balance between logical allocation and maintaining neighborly peace.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I just want everyone to feel it's fair, especially the daily commuters.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I'm leaning toward something that removes the ""fixed"" nature of the spots to stop the morning congestion.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,Let's see what the actual options are before we get too ahead of ourselves.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I agree. Let's wait for the proposals.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
46,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
47,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
48,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
49,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A could create a divide between those who can pay and those who can't. Option B is fair but temporary. Option C solves the morning rush.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Yumi,,Option A sounds great for the daily riders who are willing to pay! But Option B ensures everyone gets a turn at the dry spots.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C is the only one that actually fixes the ""shoving match"" and the rain exposure issue by making it first-come, first-served.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option A provides income for the building, which we desperately need. Option B is a bureaucratic loop. Option C is the simplest.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A is a treasurer's nightmare. Option B requires an annual event. Option C is the lowest maintenance for the association.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, if Option C is the lowest maintenance, it's the most sustainable. But will it lead to more ""leaning"" complaints?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, do you think people would actually use the double-tier racks in Option C if they are hard to use?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, it's better than fighting over a spot every morning. The physical effort of a rack is less than the stress of a conflict.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, the ""leaning"" complaints happened because there was no one to ask. In a shared system, it's just part of the deal.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, I'm strongly against Option A. We cannot add more billing hours to the treasurer's workload.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I'm worried Option B might cause tension when someone loses a spot they've had for years. Option C feels more natural.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I like the idea of the lottery in Option B because it's a fresh start for everyone every year.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,Option B doesn't solve the morning congestion. Only Option C changes the actual behavior of how we park.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Option A is the most rational for the budget, but if the administration is the bottleneck, then C is the winner.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I'm voting for C. It's the only one that doesn't create a permanent administrative burden.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"I'll vote for C. It's the most logical way to avoid long-term resentment over ""privileged"" spots.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'll go with B. I think a lottery is the kindest way to handle the shortage.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I'm voting for C. Let's end the morning shoving matches.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll vote for C. It's the most efficient and avoids the billing mess Toshio mentioned.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,pass,Toshio,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
